+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ARNA> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Norite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BALI> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Mafic and ultramafic rocks."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BHLV> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Dunite, gabbro."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BLWA> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Mafic and ultramafic rocks."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CORH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Metamafic and ultramafic rocks."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CREI> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Ortho-amphibolite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HDHS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Norite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HIO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "All components of the Caledonian Supersuite (CIGSS) that occur within the Northern Highlands and Grampian Highlands regions and formed broadly in association with the Grampian Event. This is the older (Ordovician) of the two main tectonothermal events of the Caledonian Orogeny in Scotland."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HNTL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Gabbro, peridotite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HSO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use HIO]"@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HSOMI> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete]"@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HTKN> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use HNTL, KNOC]"@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HVDD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Includes a facies with intense granite veining, and a margin facies of dolerite and gabbro."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/INSCH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Includes the Insch Upper Zone (INSUZ), Insch Middle Zone (INSMZ) and Insch Lower Zone (INSLZ) as well as unnamed units of gabbroic-rock."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/KNOC> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Gabbro, peridotite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/LGGI> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Numerous sheets of metagabbroic-rock and ortho-amphibolite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MAUDP> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Norite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MGVO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Diorite and gabbro with subsidiary serpentinite and ultramafic-rock."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MSHET> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Minor intrusions of the Shetland Islands Suite (SHEGR) not assigned to other subsuites. Includes the Yell Pegmatitic granite Vein-swarm (YPS) as well as unnamed minor intrusions of granite, felsite, mafite, microtonalite, microdiorite, dolerite, and lamprophyre."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MVCA> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Numerous mapped units of ultramafic to siliceous rocks."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEBAS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Major intrusions of the Scottish Highlands Ordovician Suite (HIO) that occur within the north-east part of the Grampian Highlands region and consist dominantly of basic rock."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NMVN> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Includes the Ronas Hill Granite Pluton (ROHG), East Northmaven Granite Sheet (EAST), Mangaster Voe Diorite-gabbro Pluton (MGVO), Roerwater Gabbro-diorite Intrusion (ROER), Hevdadale Gabbro-diorite Intrusion (HVDD), Housetter Granite Intrusion (HOUG), Ronas Voe Intrusion-breccia Intrusion Swarm (RVBR), and Muckle Row Granite Pluton (MURO) as well as other intrusions of granite, gabbro, diorite, granodiorite and ultramafic-rock."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/OBFE> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Sheets and other intrusions of agglomerate, basalt, felsite, analcime-gabbro, olivine-microgabbro and syenitic-rock."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ODMIV> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use OBFE]"@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/PTSOY> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Gabbro, serpentinite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ROER> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Includes a facies with intense granite veining, and a margin facies of dolerite and gabbro."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ROHG> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A facies of red, drusy, granophyric granite, and a facies of biotite-bearing granophyric granite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/RVBR> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Several intrusions of intrusion-breccia."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SDSTG> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Intrusions (mainly sheets) of ultramafic-rock, gabbro, diorite, granodiorite, and granite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/TRLD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Norite, gabbro."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/UDNY> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Norite, gabbro."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/YPS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Numerous veins of pegmatitic granite."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HIO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasObsoleteEquivalent> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HSO> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HNTL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasObsoleteEquivalent> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HTKN> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/KNOC> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasObsoleteEquivalent> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HTKN> .
